# The C++ is one Qt file. Left out, and why:
# - pointer-arithmetic-on-polymorphic-object crashes clang-tidy 19 on qt.cpp.
# - Qt's parent owns what `new` makes, so owning-memory and the casts Qt's
#   event and widget calls need say nothing useful here.
# - The cairo pixels the live graphs draw take a reinterpret_cast.
# - Layout pixels, short names, unbraced one-line bodies and leading return
#   types are the file's style. So are pointers tested as bools, unnamed
#   unused parameters, plain structs with public members, x and y side by
#   side, and no nodiscard.
# - Qt's headers are umbrellas, which include-cleaner can't follow.
# - The window's builders and refresh are long by nature, and there's no GSL
#   for at() on an index that isn't a constant.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-pointer-arithmetic-on-polymorphic-object,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-static-cast-downcast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-named-parameter,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '/qt\.h$'
